<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
   Governs what is allowed to leave this device. Android 12+ (this app
   targets 36) splits the two paths android:allowBackup used to cover
   together: allowBackup="false" still stops cloud backup, but on builds
   from some device manufacturers it does not stop a device to device
   transfer. With no rules file, those builds are free to carry this app's
   files to a new phone. See docs/SPEC.md §7 R20.

   Nothing here should ever travel, by either path. The SQLCipher
   passphrase is wrapped by a non exportable AndroidKeyStore key (§2,
   PassphraseProvider), which by design stays on the device that created
   it, so a copied database arrives as ciphertext the new install can
   never open. The failure mode is a first launch that cannot read its own
   database, which is worse than a clean empty start, not a data leak.

   The supported way to move to a new phone is the app's own SAF backup
   and restore (§9 #9). That path works precisely because it is not
   Keystore bound: it carries its own password, chosen by the user.

   Both sections are written out in full rather than relying on
   allowBackup="false" to cover the cloud half, so that flipping that flag
   later cannot silently re enable cloud extraction.

   That last sentence is only true from API 31 up. The platform ignores
   android:dataExtractionRules entirely below it, and this app's minSdk is
   30, so on Android 11 the flag flip this file is meant to defend against
   would have re enabled an unfiltered cloud backup with nothing to stop
   it. res/xml/backup_rules.xml is the same exclude list in the pre
   Android 12 format, wired up alongside this one via
   android:fullBackupContent, and is what makes the claim hold across the
   whole supported range. See docs/SPEC.md §7 R23.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </cloud-backup>

    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" path="." />
        <exclude domain="file" path="." />
        <exclude domain="database" path="." />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
